  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "A seafaring republic where commerce, civic ritual, and maritime law share the same tide.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Merethi bind scattered ports and islands through lighthouse oaths, harbor courts, and fiercely defended civic charters. They are open to foreign custom so long as contracts are witnessed, dues are paid, and disputes are settled under the lantern. Their captains earn respect through profitable caution rather than reckless glory, and even the poorest dock ward expects the fleet, the market, and the temple treasury to answer when storm or hunger strikes."
